course: dictionary
lesson: 8968
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word «sing» can mean making music with your voice, but it can also describe birds, kettles and the wind. The words around it show you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: Ask yourself who or what is doing the singing. If a person is singing, it probably means making music with the voice. If a bird is singing, it means making musical calls. If a kettle or the wind is singing, it means making a high, musical sound.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «That cheerful robin is also one of the fiercest birds in the garden, even singing to defend its patch.» A robin is a bird, so singing means making musical calls, and the calls warn other robins to keep away.
fact: To sing means to make music with your voice, using words or tunes.
fact: Birds sing when they make musical calls.
fact: Things like a kettle or the wind can «sing» when they make a high, musical sound.
fact: To sing someone's praises means to praise them a lot.
fact: The forms are sing, sings, sang, singing and sung.
exercise: In music lessons we sing Happy Birthday together. What does sing mean here? | To fly away quickly | *To make music with your voice | To praise someone a lot | To make a high sound like a kettle
exercise: «The kettle began to sing on the stove.» What does sing mean here? | *Makes a high, musical sound | Makes musical calls, like a bird | Makes music with the voice | Praises someone a lot
exercise: Grandma says, «Everyone sings your praises after that brilliant game.» What does sing your praises mean? | Whistles to call you home | *Praises you a lot | Sings a song for you | Sings you to sleep
test: «The wind began to sing through the trees.» What does sing mean here? | Fell asleep | *Made a high, musical sound | Sang words with a tune | Told a loud story
test: Complete the sentence: Yesterday the class ___ a song about the sea. | sings | sing | singing | *sang
exam: «The indri sings loud songs in family groups.» What does sings mean? | Praises the family a lot | *Makes loud musical calls | Whistles to call a dog | Flies in a line through the trees
